Alright — now you’re entering one of the most important OOP concepts.
And honestly, students usually confuse:

Encapsulation ❌
Abstraction ❌

So let’s separate them clearly.

🎭 What is Abstraction?
Simple Meaning

👉 Hiding implementation details and showing only essential features

User knows:

WHAT to do ✅
But not:
HOW it works internally ❌
🔥 Real-Life Example

Think about an ATM machine.

You:

insert card
enter PIN
withdraw money

But internally:

bank server
verification
database updates

👉 hidden from you

That is abstraction.

🧠 Main Goal of Abstraction
Reduce complexity
Hide unnecessary details
Make usage simple
⚠️ Difference Between Encapsulation & Abstraction
Encapsulation	Abstraction
Hides data	Hides implementation
Uses private variables	Uses abstract class/interface
Focus on security	Focus on simplicity
🧱 How Java Achieves Abstraction

Two ways:

Abstract Class
Interface (next topic)
🟢 Abstract Class

An abstract class:

cannot create objects directly
may contain abstract methods
🔥 Abstract Method

An abstract method:

has no body
child class must implement it
📦 Example
abstract class Vehicle {

    abstract void start();
}
Child Class
class Car extends Vehicle {

    void start() {
        System.out.println("Car starts with key");
    }
}
🔍 Usage
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Vehicle v = new Car();

        v.start();
    }
}
💥 What’s Happening Here?
abstract void start();

👉 Vehicle says:

“Every vehicle MUST have start()”

But:
👉 it doesn’t define HOW.

Child class decides implementation.

🧠 Why This is Powerful

Imagine:

Car starts with key
Bike starts with button
EV starts digitally

All vehicles:

have start() ✅
but implementation differs ✅

That’s abstraction + polymorphism together.

⚠️ Important Rules
❌ Cannot create object
Vehicle v = new Vehicle(); // ERROR

Because abstract class is incomplete.

✅ Child must implement abstract method

Otherwise child also becomes abstract.

🔥 Real Interview Understanding

Abstraction helps:

define common structure
force child classes to follow rules